Others’ words, and pointers at sources — quotation, citation, cross-reference, and links.

<section #ag-a | `<a>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<a>`.

<code #code:ag-a-1>
See <a https://example.com/docs | the documentation>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-a-1>
See <a https://example.com/docs | the documentation>.
</minipage>

*The positional URL form — the target is the first argument, the pipe
content is the link text. The most common authoring path. (Markdown
`[text](url)` is not an enscribe idiom; it renders as literal text.)*

</section>

<section #ag-bib-entry | `<bib-entry>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<bib-entry>`.

</section>

<section #ag-bibliography | `<bibliography>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<bibliography>`.

</section>

<section #ag-blockquote | `<blockquote>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<blockquote>`.

<code #code:ag-blockquote-1>
<quote | A short quotation.>
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-blockquote-1>
<quote | A short quotation.>
</minipage>

*The &lt;quote&gt; shorthand expands to &lt;blockquote&gt; at eHTML.*

</section>

<section #ag-cite | `<cite>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<cite>`.

<code #code:ag-cite-1>
The argument is supported by data <cite goodall2024>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-cite-1>
The argument is supported by data <cite goodall2024>.
</minipage>

*A simple citation. The resolver renders the citation according
to the document-level style. For author-year style, this becomes
"(Goodall 2024)". For numbered style, "[1]". The actual rendered
text is generated by the citation resolver, not written by the author.*

</section>

<section #ag-doi | `<doi>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<doi>`.

<code-block #code:ag-doi-1>
<meta>
  <doi | 10.1234/example.2024>
</meta>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:ag-doi-1>
<meta>
  <doi | 10.1234/example.2024>
</meta>
</minipage>

*Bare DOI as the typical authoring form.*

</section>

<section #ag-q | `<q>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<q>`.

<code #code:ag-q-1>
She said <q | hello> in passing.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-q-1>
She said <q | hello> in passing.
</minipage>

*Browsers automatically render &lt;q&gt; with quotation marks. Authors
do not include quotation marks in the content.*

</section>

<section #ag-ref | `<ref>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<ref>`.

<code #code:ag-ref-1>
See <ref @fig:scatter> for details.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-ref-1>
See <ref @fig:scatter> for details.
</minipage>

*Canonical form: @id prefix (@ references; # would declare an id on the
&lt;ref&gt; itself). The ref-resolution plugin replaces the
&lt;ref&gt; node with a __ref-marker before hast conversion. The handler
then renders an &lt;a&gt; element with computed text. Prefix word is
lowercase, from the DEFAULT_PREFIXES dictionary keyed by id prefix.*

</section>
